
🔥 Difficult DSA Problem: Trapping Rain Water
🧠 Problem Statement
Given n non-negative integers representing the height of bars, where the width of each bar is 1, compute how much water can be trapped after raining.
📌 Example
Copy code

Input: height = [4,2,0,3,2,5]
Output: 9
🖼️ Intuition (Very Important)
Water can be trapped only if there is a taller bar on both sides.
For each index i:
Copy code

Water at i =
min(max height on left, max height on right) - height[i]
If this value is negative → no water.
🚫 Brute Force (Not recommended)
For every bar, scan left and right
Time: O(n²) ❌
We need O(n) solution.
✅ Optimal Algorithm (Two Pointer Technique)
🔑 Idea
Use two pointers:
left starts at beginning
right starts at end
Maintain:
leftMax → highest bar from left
rightMax → highest bar from right
⚙️ Algorithm Steps
Initialize:
Copy code

left = 0
right = n - 1
leftMax = 0
rightMax = 0
water = 0
While left < right:
If height[left] <= height[right]:
If height[left] >= leftMax
Update leftMax
Else
Add leftMax - height[left] to water
Move left++
Else:
If height[right] >= rightMax
Update rightMax
Else
Add rightMax - height[right] to water
Move right--
